CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ anon-union member init-list takes effect: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ engaged flag initialised: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ starts disengaged: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ engaged after assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ payload holds assigned value: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[class.union.anon]: members of an anonymous union are members of the enclosing
class and may be named directly in a constructor's member-initializer list.
CBMC previously raised a CONVERSION ERROR ("found no match for symbol") for such
an initializer, and even once accepted dropped it during member-initializer
reordering.  This is the storage shape of std::optional (union payload + engaged
flag).
